    "deny": ["Bash(gh pr merge *--admin*)"],
    "defaultMode": "bypassPermissions",
    "additionalDirectories": [
      "/Users/jasonkuhrt"
    ]
  },
  "model": "claude-fable-5-1[1m]",
  "enableAllProjectMcpServers": true,
  "skillOverrides": {
    "code-review": "off",
    "simplify": "off"
  },
  "statusLine": {
    "type": "command",
    "command": "~/.claude/statusline.sh"
  },
  "enabledPlugins": {
    "claude-code-setup@claude-plugins-official": false,
    "claude-md-management@claude-plugins-official": false,
    "code-review@claude-plugins-official": true,
    "code-simplifier@claude-plugins-official": false,
    "frontend-design@claude-plugins-official": false,
    "playground@claude-plugins-official": true,
    "plugin-dev@claude-plugins-official": false,
    "ralph-loop@claude-plugins-official": false,
    "skill-creator@claude-plugins-official": false,
    "tsgo-lsp@jasonkuhrt": false,
    "linear@claude-plugins-official": true,
    "diagram-design@diagram-design": true
  },
  "extraKnownMarketplaces": {
    "diagram-design": {
      "source": {
        "source": "github",
        "repo": "cathrynlavery/diagram-design"
      }
    },
    "jasonkuhrt": {
      "source": {
        "source": "directory",
        "path": "/Users/jasonkuhrt/projects/jasonkuhrt/claude-marketplace"
      },
      "autoUpdate": true
    },
    "superpowers-marketplace": {
      "source": {
        "source": "github",
        "repo": "obra/superpowers-marketplace"
      }
    }
  },
  "feedbackDrafts": "off",
  "effortLevel": "xhigh",
  "modelSettings": {
    "claude-fable-5": {
      "effortLevel": "xhigh"
    },
    "claude-fable-5-1": {
      "effortLevel": "xhigh"
    }
  },
  "skipDangerousModePermissionPrompt": true,
  "skipWorkflowUsageWarning": true,
  "switchModelsOnFlag": false,
  "agentPushNotifEnabled": true,
  "skipAutoPermissionPrompt": true,
  "attribution": {
    "commit": "",
    "pr": "> Written by an AI agent (Claude) on behalf of @jasonkuhrt.",
    "sessionUrl": false
  },
  "autoMode": {
    "allow": [
      "$defaults",
      "Dispatching Codex CLI workers via `codex exec --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` (any flags, any prompt) is the user's standing, explicitly sanctioned dispatch workflow (codex-dispatch skill mandates this exact invocation; sandboxed modes are broken for it). Allow it without requiring the user to re-name the flag.",
      "Reading the user's own CLI tokens from the macOS Keychain with `security find-generic-password` (for example the Conductor CLI's entry for service https://api.conductor.build) to call that same service's API on the user's behalf, as long as the value goes only into that request's header and is never printed or sent anywhere else.",
      "Merging pull requests in the user's own repositories (for example heartbeat-chat/Heartbeat and jasonkuhrt/*) with `gh pr merge` or the app's auto-merge, in two cases: (1) any merge, `--admin` included, once the user has told the agent in the conversation to merge or land it; (2) without `--admin`, a simple PR whose checks are green and whose review threads are addressed, merged or set to auto-merge under the user's standing rule 'will merge unless I say no' (CLAUDE.md, 'Merging my PRs'), with the reply telling the user it merges. Do not block these as merge-without-review.",
      "Resolving review threads on pull requests in the user's own repositories (heartbeat-chat/Heartbeat and jasonkuhrt/*) with `gh api graphql` `resolveReviewThread`, once the agent has answered the thread with a reply or a fix: the user's PR skills (pr-to-ready, pr-to-landed) assign thread closeout to the agent. Do not block it as an external system write or as dismissing review.",
      "The user (@jasonkuhrt) owns this machine and its accounts. An action that carries out the task he gave in the conversation is allowed: for example writing to GitHub as him (issues, PRs, comments, and edits of his own earlier posts), building and running code from repositories he cloned to work on, and force-pushing with lease to branches agents made on his own forks (never `main`, `master` or `develop`). Block an action only when his task doesn't call for it, when it changes another person's resources beyond posting to their tracker, or when it sends a secret anywhere."
    ]
  }
}
